    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d166">

                <pb facs="0228" n="220" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg220"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/8740: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ireland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Dublin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-03-03T16:00:00+01:00">March 3, 1941—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 3—2:37 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>25. For the Under Secretary. On February 26 at my request the Prime Minister
                    received me. I set forth the substance of the Under <pb facs="0229" n="221"
                        xml:id="pg221"/> Secretary’s letter to me dated December 26, 1940, with
                    memorandum of conversations with Brennan enclosed.<anchor n="12"
                        xml:id="d166-f1"/> I pointed out I had left with the Prime Minister a copy
                    of the paraphrased text of the Under Secretary’s instructions to me dated
                    November 19<anchor n="13" xml:id="d166-f2"/> when he received me on November 22
                    and that this text would obviously be conclusive as to what Mr. Welles said. The
                    paraphrased text was produced from the files and he suggested that a
                    misunderstanding must have arisen as between Brennan and his office. I made no
                    comment on this point. He did not suggest that I had attempted to alter the text
                    in conversation and accepted without objection the letter which I handed him and
                    which he read in my presence giving my view of the transaction.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gray</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d166-f1" n="12" xml:id="d166-f1-content">
                <p>The memoranda referred to are those of November 9 and December 9, <ref
                        target="frus1940v03#pg_166"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>,
                        1940, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>, pp. 166</ref> and <ref
                        target="frus1940v03#pg_173">173</ref>, respectively; Under Secretary’s
                    letter not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d166-f2" n="13" xml:id="d166-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram No. 77, November 19, 6 p.m., <ref target="frus1940v03#pg_171"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">ibid</hi>., p. 171</ref>.</p>
            </note>
